## Build from an empty working directory

Prerequisites: Node.js 24 and npm, with a C++ build toolchain if the platform
has no better-sqlite3 prebuilt binary. Dependency versions and integrity values
are pinned by package-lock.json. No cloud account or credentials are required.
The following is an inert recipe to qualify after source/package freeze, not
an execution record or installation approval. Once the exact source package
and prerequisites are independently qualified, its intended commands are:

```sh
npm ci --ignore-scripts
npm run build:engine
npm test
```

The build compiles src/ to dist/src/, verifies the static minifier, copies
vendor/ into dist/vendor/, and imports the actual renderer and compiler.
Earlier package checks reused installed dependency bytes. They do not qualify
a clean installation, native module availability or a build for the current
source. Each platform and exact locked dependency set needs its own check.
The intended build receipt is .runtime/browser-build.json. Its provenance
helper accepts HANDOVER-MANIFEST.json without an own Git checkout; an actual
no-Git build of the current frozen package still needs its execution receipt.

`npm test` here is deliberately a package smoke check, not the development
repository's complete test suite. It opens the included synthetic deck, renders
a card and checks the license and runtime assets. It does not establish full
Ruby parity, hosted runtime support, or migration acceptance.

## Run locally

Prepare a disposable copy of the synthetic deck and its files. This also
applies the data-version migration the renderer needs. Start the Node host
with the copy's path and an unused port:

```sh
node tools/handover/prepare-demo.mjs
node vm-staging-server.mjs ./tmp/demo/deck.sqlite3 3100
```

The held recipe is intended for a loopback host. Health, Home and graceful
shutdown must be checked against the frozen host's actual control protocol;
the older HTTP recipe is not current host/lifecycle acceptance. Never point
this review host at a production database.
The preparation command copies the synthetic deck's files beside its database
and refuses to overwrite an existing demo. Hosting and deployment configuration are
outside this local review package; no command above creates cloud resources.

`node tools/handover/verify-local-host.mjs` is the held local-check helper;
its compatibility with the frozen host and successful child cleanup require
their own execution receipt. It was not run for the current preparation.

## Local migration and recovery

Importer and recovery source is retained under tools/migrate/.
Read docs/handover/MIGRATION.md and docs/migration-recovery.md before using them.
Recovery operates on isolated SQLite copies and upload trees, refuses existing
restore destinations and preserves the failed target for reconciliation.
Database and file writers must be paused for the snapshot; this is not an
atomic live backup across both stores. Private inputs and their generated
snapshots must stay outside the proposed source package.

The development tests cited by those documents are not this package's smoke
suite. Local synthetic checks do not establish a complete private-deck migration,
original-user-password access, hosted providers, real attachments or a cutover.

## Reproduce comparisons

The intended snapshot selects the reference harness and its synthetic-v1 and
write-battery-v1 decks. After final freeze and a qualified build, its intended
diagnostic commands are:

```sh
node reference-harness/runner/run.mjs --adapter reference-harness/adapters/ts/adapter.json --fixture reference-harness/fixtures/synthetic-v1 --out tmp/reference-run
node reference-harness/runner/grade.mjs --fixture reference-harness/fixtures/synthetic-v1 --actual tmp/reference-run --diagnostic
```

For a source-only snapshot without an own Git checkout, this command requests
diagnostic comparison explicitly; it cannot produce a candidate or
release pass. A release checkout must separately supply its exact full
candidate commit to the source-qualifying checker. Read the raw report for rendering, semantics, persistence and side effects
separately, including failures and skipped operations. Comparison rules are in
reference-harness/SPEC.md and NORMALIZATION-EVIDENCE.md. Captured expectations
are evidence for their fixed synthetic deck, not all existing decks.
Fixture directories deliberately withheld pending disclosure are excluded from
this package. A runner naming those missing steps is reporting unexecuted
coverage, not a successful check of those steps.

## Review order and privacy

Read PORT-SCOPE.md, DIFFERENCES.md, RUBY-MAP.md, then source and NOTICE.
When generated by the current writer, HANDOVER-MANIFEST.json inventories every
packaged file with original Git mode, byte size and SHA-256. Windows mode
metadata does not establish native POSIX permission preservation.
Its sourceCommit names the packaging commit and engineCommit names the separately
designated integrated engine checkpoint. These are distinct source identities.
No .git directory or development commit history is included. Private history
was not rewritten. The package scanner is a pattern check, not a guarantee that
arbitrary secrets or real-deck data are absent; independent content and license
review remains required before this exact snapshot can be approved for sharing.
